Z||000000||Manta||05-20-2000||01:22 PM||||1986 1/2 Fiero GT. 2.8 liter V6. 80,000 miles. Not much wrong except the Speedometer, Odometer and Cruise Control do not work. I checked the Vehicle Speed Sensor and it puts out A.C. Volts and max. out at 4.95 Vac at high R.P.M s. (That's Normal, Right?)<BR>I then swaped out the gauge cluster and still nothing.  <P>NEW UPDATE: This is getting strange.I just got back from a 500 mile 2 day drive. at about 250 miles everything started working. I didn't hit any rough roads or bumps. Then of all things 34 miles later I got a hole on a radiator hose and the engine got realy hot.While I was coasting a half mile to a rest area the speedo stopped reading then started then stopped about 5 times then dead again.I taped up the hose and drove it the other 250 miles but it never came on again.<BR>Could the heat of the engine knock out anything that controls the speedo or would it have gone out at that point anyway?<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Phaeton||05-20-2000||02:49 PM||||Bad grounds? Ign/start switch on column? Thermal expansion/contraction can sometimes affect borderline connections.<BR>Electical problems are the Devil's own handiwork.||||reg||12
